# L §5.18 example ask q3, copied (npv a def of 0 PLN, rate an input): F(v) = npv - 0 PLN = 0 at lo, and step 1 says
# "If F(lo) = 0 the answer is lo": 0 %/year, which prints as a decimal with its period (L §5.18 Output: "never as
# %").  The pin of v isn't in the register.
=== m.tally
model t
  tally 2
  on 2026-12-31
  start 2026-01-01
  end 2026-12-31

source s "s"
unit PLN: currency minor 0.01

kind accounts_pl: place PLN signed
input rec_total[x in accounts_pl, m in months]: money PLN
input rate: rate
def npv: money PLN = 0 PLN
def free_cash[m in months]: money PLN = 0 PLN

ask q3: solve npv == 0 PLN for rate in [0 %/year, 20 %/year] to 0.0001 %/year law 2026-06-30
=== expect
q3: 0 /year
  law date 2026-06-30, cut 2026-12-31
